<section id="measuring-distance" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="measuring-distance">Measuring Distance</h2>
<p>The k-mer frequencies are represented as 4<sup>k</sup>-dimensional vectors. We can estimate the similarity of two genomes by computing a distance metric using their <em>k</em>-mer vectors. To remove the influence of genome size to the computed distance, we first normalize the elements then compute the L2 distance, also known as the Euclidean distance. I’ve packaged our previously implemented functions into a convenience class called <code>KmerSet</code>.</p>
<div id="kmer-distance-function" class="cell" data-execution_count="6">
