<span id="cb2-23">            dist <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span> distance.cityblock(counts1, counts2)</span>
<span id="cb2-24">        <span class="cf" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-weight: bold;
font-style: inherit;">case</span> _:</span>
<span id="cb2-25">            dist <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span> distance.euclidean(counts1, counts2)</span>
<span id="cb2-26"></span>
<span id="cb2-27">    <span class="cf" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-weight: bold;
font-style: inherit;">return</span> dist</span></code></pre></div>
</div>
<p>Computing the distances between pairwise comparisons of three Influenza genomes, we get the matrix in Figure&nbsp;3.</p>
<div id="cell-fig-distance-matrix" class="cell" data-execution_count="7">
<div class="cell-output cell-output-display">
<div id="fig-distance-matrix" class="quarto-float quarto-figure quarto-figure-center anchored">
<figure class="quarto-float quarto-float-fig figure">
<div aria-describedby="fig-distance-matrix-caption-0ceaefa1-69ba-4598-a22c-09a6ac19f8ca">
<img src="/posts/kmer-analysis/index_files/figure-html/fig-distance-matrix-output-1.png" class="img-fluid figure-img">
</div>
<figcaption class="quarto-float-caption-bottom quarto-float-caption quarto-float-fig" id="fig-distance-matrix-caption-0ceaefa1-69ba-4598-a22c-09a6ac19f8ca">
Figure&nbsp;3: Distance matrix of three Influenza genomes
</figcaption>
</figure>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>The low distance values show the relatedness of the three genomes. This makes sense as all genomes are derived from the Influenza virus. However, we are still able to detect subtle differences between genomes by virtue of their <em>k</em>-mer compositions. Using the distances, we can conclude that Influenza A (<em>GCA_000865725</em>) has a genome that is more akin to Influenza C (<em>GCA_000856665</em>).</p>


</section>

 ]]></description>
