<section id="hello-there" class="level1">
<h1>Hello there!</h1>
<p>I am <strong>Jan</strong>, the sole author of this website. I finished my undergraduate degree in Biology and currently doing my masters in Bioinformatics. I work as a research associate for a clinical study on diabetic foot ulcers. My main role revolves around thermal imaging of wounds of diabetic patients. Later on, I’ll be constructing and analyzing the proteomes derived from exudate samples at different stages of healing. Outside of work, I run a small, family-owned business where I wear many hats as co-owner, software developer, and business analyst. In my free time, I like to watch movies and read books. I have a keen liking towards games and programming.</p>
<p>BioByte is a blogging website focusing on topics in <strong>computational biology</strong>, <strong>bioinformatics</strong>, <strong>data science</strong>, and <strong>programming</strong>. It is intended to be my personal notebook for learning new topics and concepts in previously mentioned fields. As much as possible, I try to make each blog independent from all others. Written proses will be related with one another through links when appropriate.</p>
<p>I will be covering topics in:</p>
<ul>
<li>Genomics and Proteomics</li>
<li>Computational Biology</li>
<li>AI and Machine Learning</li>
<li>Computer Vision</li>
<li>Data Science</li>
<li>any many other (hopefully related) topics!</li>
</ul>
<p>Feel free to reach out thru my email at <a href="mailto:jegsamson.dev@gmail.com">jegsamson.dev@gmail.com</a>. You can also find my personal GitHub account <a href="https://github.com/dagsdags212">here</a>.</p>


